<p>Dear Mr. Kozin,</p>
<p>Further to my email of November 2, I now have a second quotation for the=
 UAE filing agent, and a recommendation on the searching authority.</p>
<p><b>Second agent option.</b> Saba IP, a long-established regional intelle=
ctual property firm with an office in Dubai, has confirmed that it is regis=
tered with the UAE Ministry of Economy and can file the applications for PB=
K. Its fee is USD 1,500 per application.
 That fee includes the filing and handling of all communications through th=
e international phase. Saba would also give me full ownership access to the=
 applications in WIPO's online system, so I could receive all notices direc=
tly and make formal corrections
 myself without additional agent fees. As with AGIP, no power of attorney i=
s needed, and Saba would invoice PBK directly with payment in advance.</p>
<p>By comparison, AGIP's fee is USD 787.50 per application including VAT, w=
ith USD 750 plus VAT for each correction or reply it files. AGIP is the low=
er-cost choice; Saba includes more of the post-filing handling. Either is s=
uitable. I am waiting for both firms
 to confirm the name and registration number of the individual agent who wi=
ll sign the filings, and I will send these to you as soon as I receive them=
.</p>
<p><b>Searching authority.</b> For a UAE applicant, the Korean Intellectual=
 Property Office is also available as the international searching authority=
. Its search fee for an English-language application is currently CHF 688, =
compared with CHF 1,239 for the
 Australian Office, a saving of about CHF 550 per application. Its searches=
 are well regarded, and it is typically faster. I now recommend the Korean =
Office, unless you prefer the Australian Office for a particular reason.</p=
>
<p><b>Your decision.</b> To proceed, I need your written choice of agent (A=
GIP or Saba), your approval to give that firm PBK's name for its conflict c=
heck, and your choice of searching authority. Please also let me know wheth=
er you accept my proposal of October
 27, so that I can begin work. The December 11 statutory deadline for Group=
 2 leaves limited time, so I would be grateful for your reply this week.</p=
>
<p>Kind regards,</p>
<p>Michael L. Bartholomew<br>
Bartholomew Law PC<br>
Registered U.S. Patent Attorney, USPTO Reg. No. 60,225<br>
Highland, UT 84003 =EF=BF=BD Office 385.230.5310</p>
